    "body": "The compiler directives list in `docs/src/userguide/source_files_and_compilation.rst` says `unraisable_tracebacks` has `default=False`, but the default has been `True` since 0.26:\n\n- `Cython/Compiler/Options.py:233` in `_directive_defaults`: `'unraisable_tracebacks': True,`\n- `CHANGES.rst` (0.26): \"The ``unraisable_tracebacks`` option now defaults to ``True``.\"\n\nThis changes the one occurrence to `*default=True*`. Docs only.\n\nFound with AI assistance (Claude Code) while comparing the documented directive defaults against `_directive_defaults`; this was the only mismatch.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
    "closed_at": null,
